==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|по́ѣздъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
According to Dal, from {{m+|ru|пое́здка|t=trip, journey}} and originally meaning a series of wagons following each other, a meaning preserved in {{m|ru|сва́дебный по́езд|t=wedding train (procession)}}. Cognates include {{cog|pl|pojazd}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|по́езд}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-поезд.ogg}}

===Noun===
[[Image:2M62M-1198 Kyviskes-Kena.jpg|thumb|поезд]]
{{ru-noun+|c|по́езд|(1)|adj=поездно́й}}

# {{lb|ru|railroads}} [[train]], a [[line]] of [[connected]] [[railway]] [[car]]s
#: {{uxi|ru|[[е́здить]] [[на]] '''по́езде'''|to go (or travel) by train}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[скоростно́й]] '''по́езд'''|bullet train}}
# {{lb|ru|dated}} [[caravan]], [[convoy]], [[procession]]
# {{lb|ru|regional}} a [[method]] of [[fishing]], in which a [[fishing]] [[net]] is [[pull]]ed by [[two]] [[side-by-side]] [[boat]]s
# {{lb|ru|regional}} a [[net]] used for this method of fishing

